  "caption": "Quinn lost a fight to a pickle jar, then read that grip strength is a health marker. Is it a big deal?\n\nGrip is easy to measure and often reflects whole-body strength and muscle reserve, which can help you recover from illness, surgery or a fall. The good news: it can improve at any age.\n\nWhat often helps: whole-body strength training at least twice a week, farmer's carries, treating hand grippers as an extra rather than the main plan, and tracking your trend and left-right balance over time.\n\nA sudden or one-sided loss of grip, or weakness with numbness or tingling, is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
